**/build/
**/out/
**/CMakeUserPresets.json
.claude/
.vs/

# Node / TypeScript
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/generated-ts/
**/src/generated/
**/package-lock.json

# Local caches used by integration tests (e.g. downloaded protoc binaries)
**/.cache/

# Conan-generated build/run environment scripts (VirtualBuildEnv / VirtualRunEnv).
# Conan writes these env launchers into the recipe's base folder whenever
# conan install/build/create runs there directly; transient, never source.
**/conanbuild.sh
**/conanbuild.bat
**/conanrun.sh
**/conanrun.bat
**/conanbuildenv-*
**/conanrunenv-*
**/deactivate_conanbuild.*
**/deactivate_conanrun.*

# Log files
*.log
debug.log

# The licence files cd.protoc stages into the npm shim before publishing (BIND-9b-7,
# review T13, M6): copies of ci.protoc's artifact, never tracked here.
protoc/npm/LICENSE
protoc/npm/COPYING
protoc/npm/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt

# .NET build output (dotnet/). Scoped to that directory rather than a bare
# **/bin/: protoc/npm/bin/protoc-gen-fletcher.js is a tracked launcher script,
# and a blanket rule would quietly stop tracking it.
#
# packages.lock.json is deliberately NOT ignored — unlike package-lock.json
# above, it is what makes CI's locked-mode restore a guard rather than a
# formality, so it belongs in the tree.
dotnet/**/bin/
dotnet/**/obj/
dotnet/**/*.user
# BenchmarkDotNet writes its reports beside the project it runs from. The numbers
# that matter are transcribed into c-abi/benchmarks/README.md with their method.
dotnet/**/BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/

# The binding ABI conformance suite's C# half lives under integration-tests/,
# so the rules above do not reach it. Scoped the same way, and for the same
# reason: a blanket **/bin/ would quietly stop tracking the protoc launcher.
integration-tests/**/dotnet/**/bin/
integration-tests/**/dotnet/**/obj/
# Eiva.Fletcher.Protoc's pack project (BIND-9b-5), scoped for the same reason.
protoc/nuget/bin/
protoc/nuget/obj/
integration-tests/**/dotnet/**/*.user
dotnet/**/TestResults/
dotnet/artifacts/
# Benchmark consumer lockfile: `conan lock create` regenerates it from the local cache before each
# run and the revisions it pins exist only in that cache; the recorded runs name them in README.md.
arrow-bridge/benchmarks/conan.lock

# The MicroXRCEAgent the transport-conformance lane builds on Linux (D-BIND-56).
integration-tests/pubsub-transport-conformance/agent/install/
